\ Bounded-memory regression for a `once` definition made inside a word body.
\
\ `;` used to allocate the cell, its name, and its guard on the state target's arena, and to list the
\ cell for teardown. Each call into the word then kept all of it until exit. The loops below exhausted
\ the 4 MB cap in the `.flags` sidecar within a few thousand calls. A cell made in a transient frame is
\ owned by that frame and dies with its last reference, so every loop stays flat.

plain: ( -- n ) [
  c: once ( -- n ) [ 42 ] ;
  c
] ;

captures: ( n -- n ) [
  x: swap ;
  c: once ( -- n ) [ x 1 + ] ;
  c c +
] ;

typed-string: ( -- s ) [
  c: once ( -- s ) [ "hello" ] ;
  c
] ;

20000 [ plain drop ] times
10000 [ 1 captures drop ] times
10000 [ typed-string drop ] times

"flat" print-line
